# Patch 0014 — Remove the experimental code-mode tool
#
# Purpose: Delete the experimental code-mode tool in full. The tool
# (id "execute") ran a confined orchestration script against
# connected MCP tools through the @opencode-ai/codemode interpreter.
# It was off by default, gated by the OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_CODE_MODE
# runtime flag, but its dynamic import kept the interpreter and the
# TypeScript compiler (imported only by that interpreter) inside
# every shipped binary — about 3.7 MiB of bundle. With the tool gone,
# MCP tools are always listed to the model individually, which is
# the behavior the default configuration already had. The codemode
# workspace package and the dependency declarations stay; the bundle
# loses them through reachability alone.
#
# Upstream files:
#   - packages/opencode/src/tool/code-mode.ts (deleted)
#   - packages/opencode/src/tool/registry.ts (flag-gated dynamic
#     import, the conditional execute tool entry, the catalog
#     description plumbing, and the builtin list entry removed)
#   - packages/opencode/src/session/tools.ts (the code-mode early
#     return that hid individual MCP tools removed)
#   - packages/opencode/src/effect/runtime-flags.ts
#     (experimentalCodeMode flag removed)
#   - packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx (the dedicated
#     execute tool renderer removed; historical parts fall back to
#     the generic renderer)
#   - Tests: test/tool/code-mode.test.ts and
#     code-mode-integration.test.ts deleted; registry tests lose the
#     two enabled-flag cases and keep asserting no execute tool is
#     exposed.
#
# Rebase note: registry.ts is moderate traffic; the deletions are
# mechanical (remove the import of ./code-mode and every "execute"
# special case). If upstream renames the tool id, re-apply by
# deleting the same wiring under the new id.
